      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-22T17:45:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we think doing a swizzle manually is slower than the cast on GPUs that don\u0027t have this bug?\n\nWhat happens if we write another shader that tries to do this same cast? What if someone who is a client writes the same cast in their code?\n\nIMO I think we have a few options:\n1) Ignore this bug\n2) SkSL removes support for this cast all together\n3) SkSL supplies a workaround in the compiler for old GPUs.",
      "parentUuid": "91918cf4_559a1cae",
      "revId": "ef3db3b50efe5fe8c4abc033b3c6e966e5848735",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d3ebafd_f27696a9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-22T17:50:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I *strongly* suspect that the performance of `mat2(v4)` is identical to `mat2(v4.xy, v4.zw)`. I do not expect to see any measurable difference at all and I expect a compiler actually converts the first form to the second form internally during compilation. \n\nIf you feel that a workaround in the compiler is necessary, we can do it, but it\u0027ll be a lot more complex than this and is more likely to _actually_ incur overhead in real shaders.",
      "parentUuid": "d9af60a2_452eb159",
      "revId": "ef3db3b50efe5fe8c4abc033b3c6e966e5848735",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
